{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1507370-trinity-pre-modern-nobels-as-characters","id":1507370,"title":"[Trinity] Pre-modern Nobels as characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-03T21:23:41-07:00","id":1507370,"title":"[Trinity] Pre-modern Nobels as characters","content":"Before 20th century - and some say to this day - Nobility was social class above all other society. I wonder how would you reflect that in characters of <b>Trinity Continuum</b>, with more and more historical eras we got.<br /> <br /> You think simply <i>Life of Privilege</i> Origin path is enough? Maybe some new Path or Edge should be made? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T03:27:08-07:00","id":1507388,"title":"","content":"I think you should create a separate Path if you\u2019re doing medieval or Renaissance nobles. But then again you\u2019d probably need a whole separate game line to cover those time periods too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T03:41:32-07:00","id":1507390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1507370-trinity-pre-modern-nobels-as-characters?p=1507388#post1507388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you should create a separate Path if you\u2019re doing medieval or Renaissance nobles. But then again you\u2019d probably need a whole separate game line to cover those time periods too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded! Actual working Feudal Nobles managing large estates and running a millitary are profoundly different from post-Westphalian Aristocrats living as courtiers and political functionaries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T03:46:33-07:00","id":1507391,"title":"","content":"Life of Privilege as origin is a good start. Then add a charismatic leader or a military related as role and as society add the court / house / dynasty related, add money to that (Wealth edge) and you are done.<br /> <br /> The paths are probably the best aspect to give them the feeling, because the path will give them access to a lot of things (contacts, material, troops, etc.) as they raise their \u201cstatus\u201d (dots). A king should have the 3 paths at 3+ dots to represent his political and personal power, specially his own house path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T07:40:41-07:00","id":1507401,"title":"","content":"Honestly, for Aether a Origin Path for former nobility would work really well. A LOT of monarchies ended in the 19th century as revolution or consolidation into larger states happened. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> mentioned I don't think you can create a one size fits all Path for aristocracy though. Even something as basic as the skills are going to vary wildly, and Edges more so. I know people have thrown around Wealth as an obvious Edge choice, but like a driving factor in the history of Europe was that the nobility was usually broke as hell and deeply in debt but wanted to do expensive things like go to war or become emperor of the Holy Roman Empire. Mercenaries are expensive, even levied troops generally want to be paid or they tend to use all the weapons and combat experience they have to rebel.<br /> <br /> It's a very cool idea, but it makes the most sense to make custom Paths the fit the time period, or go for a heavily romanticized version (which works very well for TC).<br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Romanticized Nobility Path</span></u><br /> <b>Skills</b>: Close Combat, Culture, Command, Integrity<br /> <b>Possible Connections</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Community</b>: The holding or court they're most associated with and draw their rights and privileges from<br /> <b>Access</b>: Justice of the king, taxes, loans, levied troops, gifts from ambitious courtiers, gifts from a social superior that come with certain strings attached<br /> <b>Contacts</b>: A trustworthy seneschal, the pope, the anti-pope, a learned scholar, your spouse, an ambitious fellow noble</div> <b>Edges</b>: Patron \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022, Fame \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022, Skilled Liar \u2022\u2022, Wealth \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Striking \u2022\u2022","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T08:08:58-07:00","id":1507407,"title":"","content":"I think we must keep in mind each character have at least 3 paths, with each one and the combination of the 3 being the defining \u201carchetype\u201d of the character.<br /> <br /> If it was up to me to create paths, I would go for an origin path like Court-dweller, as a catch all people that grew on the castles and palaces, even the ones with minor titles. It would be very close to Life of privilege, with more focus on the social interaction and lore related to the families and history.<br /> <br /> From there we have more than a few options that are largely covered in the roles, military tacticians, leaders, knights, explorers, etc, many options.<br /> <br /> And the last would be a lot of different paths for the different societies/houses. Let\u2019s say a path for each great house in Dune or GoT, and a path for each Minor house. That would be very specific for the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T10:57:41-07:00","id":1507420,"title":"","content":"I see four main realistic noble types.<br /> <br /> From the &quot;Dark Ages&quot; to the &quot;High Middle Ages&quot; Nobles would mainly be a sort of mafiosa. A baron and his knights would mainly be a gang. <br /> <br /> The &quot;High Middle Ages &quot; until the end of &quot;Dog Feudalism&quot; (a transitional period between Feudalism and Capitalism) the millitary man managing estates would be the norm.<br /> <br /> The early modern Aristocracy gets you the courtier Nobles. <br /> <br /> The 19th and 20th centuries gets you Nobles as Celebrities. Movie Stars and other show people kick them out of this role.<br /> <br /> Each period has scads of exceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}